      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Anglican Church of the Holy Spirit began in 1977, with a small congregation meeting in the Algester State School library.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algester%2C_Queensland",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Algester was heavily developed from the mid‑1970s onward, transforming from virgin bushland into a bustling suburb.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algester%2C_Queensland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1979 a kit home was built on Algester Road as a rectory, with the first service held on 21 October and the first baptism on 4 November.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algester%2C_Queensland",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The new church building on Algester Road was officially dedicated on 18 October 1981, after the foundation stone was laid by Archbishop John Grindrod in July.",
